  funding-text = {INUIT (Ice Nuclei research UnIT) is a multiinstitutional project (FOR1525, https://www.ice-nuclei.de/, last access: 20 March 2019) funded by the German Research Foundation (DFG). The objective of INUIT is to comprehensively study the atmospheric heterogeneous ice formation with collaboration among various research institutions. All INUIT members and associated partners acknowledge Birte Hulsen und Susanne Staechelin for central coordination and administration of the INUIT research unit. We thank Shaul Lapidot, Clarite Azerraf and Melodea Ltd. for providing the NCC samples for this research. The AIDA team (Ottmar Mohler and Naruki Hiranuma) and the INKA team (Kristina Hohler and Thea Schiebel) acknowledge the IMK-AAF engineering and infrastructure group (Georg Scheurig, Rainer Buschbacher, Tomasz Chudy, Olga Dombrowski, Jens Nadolny, Frank Schwarz and Steffen Vogt) for their continued support throughout INUIT-1 and INUIT-2. The CSU-CFDC team (Kaitlyn Suski, Gregg P. Schill and Paul J. DeMott) acknowledges the US National Science Foundation (NSF) for support from grant AGS1358495. Gregg P. Schill additionally acknowledges support from NSF postdoctoral grant AGS1433517. The CNR-ISAC team acknowledges funding for their research from the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme FP7-ENV-2013 project BACCHUS (grant no. 603445) and Franco Corticelli (Institute for Microelectronics and Microsystems IMM-CNR) for SEM observations. The FRIDGE group acknowledges funding by DFG in the Research Unit FOR 1525 (INUIT) under BI 462/3-2. For the LACIS work, Heike Wex was funded within the INUIT subproject WE 4722/1-2. The MRI cloud simulation chamber experiments were partly supported by JSPS KAKENHI grant numbers 23244095 and 17H00787. Support of the PNNL-CIC work for Gourihar Kulkarni was provided by the U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) Office of Biological and Environmental Research (OBER) Atmospheric Research Systems Program (ASR). The Pacific Northwest Nationa