  note = {14th Topical Seminar on Innovative Particle and Radiation Detectors, Siena, ITALY, OCT 03-06, 2016},
  abstract = {Operational experience with the recently upgraded irradiation facility at the University of Birmingham is presented. This is based around the high intensity area of the MC40 medical cyclotron providing proton energies between 3 and 38 MeV and currents ranging from tens of fA to mu A. Accurate dosimetry for displacement damage and total ionizing dose, using a combination of techniques, is offered. Irradiations are carried out in a temperature controlled chamber that can be scanned through the beam, with the possibility for the devices to be biased, clocked, and read-out. Fluence up to several 10(16) 1 MeV n(eq)/cm(2) and GRad ionizing dose can be delivered within a day.},
